# Language models
- 08 bow: each position averages all earlier positions (causal mask)
- 09 self-attention: learned weighted average (q/k/v), positional embeddings
- 10 transformer: multi-head, feed-forward, residual, layernorm, stacked blocks
- 11 bpe: tokenizer (train merges, encode, decode)
- 12 gpt: transformer on bpe tokens, scaled up, temperature / top-k sampling

# Encoders (on top of 12)
- 13 encoder: drop the causal mask, train with masked-token prediction (bert style)
- 14 embedding model: pool tokens into one vector, contrastive loss on pairs, matryoshka dims (embeddinggemma style)
- 15 decision model: system 1, following the jeva paper (arxiv 2610.18773)
  - encode the request and each option separately with the 13 encoder (options never see each other -> no order bias)
  - one decision block: request attends over the options, score = dot(request, option), softmax picks one
  - coverage gate: "none of these options fits" probability
  - typed outputs: choice, yes/no, score
  - calibration: check that 0.9 confidence is right 90% of the time

# Mixture of experts (on top of 12)
- 16 moe: several feed-forward experts + softmax router (every expert used)
- 17 topk moe: route each token to top-k experts + load-balancing loss
- 18 shared moe: always-on shared experts + routed experts
- 19 upcycling: start an moe from a trained dense gpt's feed-forward weights
- 20 multi-token prediction: extra heads predicting t+2, t+3 (works on dense or moe)

# Generative models (images, independent of the above)
- 21 vae: encoder -> latent -> decoder, reparameterisation, kl loss
- 22 gan: generator vs discriminator

# Reinforcement learning
- 23 rl: policy gradient (reinforce) on a small toy environment
- 24 sft: fine-tune gpt on prompt -> answer pairs
- 25 rl gpt: policy gradient on gpt with a checkable reward (grpo style)
- 26 thinking gpt: reward correct final answers, let it learn to reason first
- 27 rl moe: rl on the moe model, routing stability
